<section class="phero"><div class="phero-media"><img src="/assets/img/photos/consultation.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/consultation-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/consultation.webp 960w" sizes="100vw" width="960" height="640" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/claim-worksheets/">Worksheets</a></li><li aria-current="page">Appraisal Readiness Check</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">Free checklist</p><h1>Appraisal Readiness Check</h1><p class="lede">Appraisal rewards preparation. Answer ten questions to see how ready your file is and what to gather before you invoke the clause.</p></div></section>
<section class="sec tool-sec"><div class="wrap"><div class="rv">
<div class="tool" data-tool="ready">
  <div class="tool-head"><span>Appraisal readiness check</span><i>10 quick questions</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <ul class="quiz"><li data-w="3" data-fix="Request the complete line-item estimate from your adjuster."><span>I have the insurer’s full, itemized estimate (not just the payment letter).</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get a detailed, itemized estimate from a licensed contractor or independent estimator."><span>I have my own contractor or independent estimate covering the same scope.</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Confirm coverage in writing. Appraisal resolves amount, not coverage."><span>The insurer has accepted that the loss is covered.</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Gather every photo and video you have and note the dates."><span>I have dated photos of the damage taken before repairs or cleanup.</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find the “Appraisal” paragraph in your policy form and read it closely."><span>I’ve read the appraisal clause in my policy.</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Use the claim deadline calendar and confirm dates with your policy."><span>I know my policy deadlines (proof of loss, depreciation recovery, suit limitation).</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Collect receipts for tarps, drying, board-up and other emergency work."><span>I’ve kept receipts for temporary repairs and mitigation.</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Run the claim gap and fee estimator to see if the gap justifies appraisal."><span>The gap between the two estimates is more than a few thousand dollars.</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Use the wind vs. flood split estimator and document water lines."><span>I’ve separated wind damage from any flood damage (coastal properties).</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Download or request your current declarations page."><span>I have the declarations page showing my limits and deductibles.</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li></ul>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="btn ghost small" data-reset>Reset answers</button></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out" aria-live="polite">
      <div class="gauge"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="50" cy="50" r="40" class="g-bg"/><circle cx="50" cy="50" r="40" class="g-arc" data-o="arc"/></svg><div><b data-o="score">–</b><small>Score</small></div></div>
      <p class="out-msg" data-o="verdict"></p>
      <div class="out-rows"><div><span>Answered</span><b data-o="count">0 / 10</b></div></div>
      <p class="todo-h">Still to do</p>
      <ul class="todo" data-o="todo"></ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></div>
<p class="tool-note">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms. They aren’t a quote, an appraisal or legal advice, and nothing you enter is stored.</p></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>What the score means</h2>
<p>Each question is weighted by how much it affects an appraisal outcome. The itemized estimates and coverage acceptance carry the most weight, because without them appraisal can’t really work. A high score means you have what a panel expects to see; a low score gives you a to-do list.</p>
<h2>Why preparation matters</h2>
<p>An appraisal award is binding on the amount of loss once two of three panel members sign. If key evidence is missing, the award may lock in a lower number than the damage deserves. It’s much easier to gather documents before appraisal than to argue about them after.</p>
<p>Your answers are not saved or sent anywhere.</p>
<h2>Questions about this worksheet</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Do I need a perfect score to invoke appraisal?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. But each “no” answer is a gap a panel may notice. Close the important ones first.</p></div></details><details><summary>Why is coverage acceptance on the list?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Appraisal decides the amount of loss, not coverage. If coverage is denied, you may need an attorney instead.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is my information stored?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. The checklist runs entirely in your browser.</p></div></details></div><h2>More free worksheets</h2><div class="cards cards-3"><a class="card card-tool rv" href="/claim-worksheets/wind-vs-flood-split-estimator/"><span class="card-media"><img src="/assets/img/photos/flood-street.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/flood-street-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/flood-street.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1100px) 50vw, 380px" width="1024" height="683" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="card-tag">Estimator</span></span><span class="card-body"><h3 class="card-t">Wind vs. Flood Split Estimator</h3><span class="card-p">See how the wind-versus-flood allocation changes what your homeowners and flood policies each pay.</span><span c